<GuideLayout
  title="Studio-to-Street Luxury Trends in Activewear"
  type="TREND REPORT"
  description="How studio-to-street luxury trends are shaping activewear design, fabric selection, color planning and private label collection strategy."
>
  <p>Studio-to-street activewear sits between workout clothing and lifestyle fashion. Customers want leggings, bras, jackets and sets that perform in training but still look polished for daily wear.</p>

  <h2>Design Signals</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Clean silhouettes with fewer visible seams.</li>
    <li>Soft compression fabrics with premium hand feel.</li>
    <li>Neutral color systems with seasonal accent tones.</li>
    <li>Minimal logos, tonal branding and subtle hardware.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Fabric Direction</h2>
  <p>Brands often choose nylon-spandex blends, brushed finishes, interlock constructions and sculpting fabrics for this category. The goal is comfort, shape and visual refinement.</p>

  <h2>Collection Planning Advice</h2>
  <p>Start with a tight capsule: leggings, sports bra, jacket and one lifestyle bottom. This gives the brand a complete look without overloading inventory.</p>
</GuideLayout>
